      "id": "thm-ams-ergodic-information-aep",
      "location": "3.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "[F4] says that under the stationary mean, normalized cylinder self-information converges almost surely to h. Step 3.1 then claims that intersecting the shifts of this full-measure set establishes the SMB limit along the moving starts k(n). The intersection gives convergence for each fixed shift; it does not establish convergence when the shift varies with n. The condition (n-k(n))/n→1 does not supply that missing uniformity, and step 5.1 relies on the suffix limit. A moving-start argument is needed.",
